:55.6,"_gate_spread":-0.05613803337356536,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.7247261187395774,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":100.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.1103831016431943,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":70.1,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.08211355182330116,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":66.1,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.26181843568864505,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.053414468882811095,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.09616077243858026,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.118030004,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":78.7,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"GoodRx Holdings, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, offers information and tools that enable consumers to compare prices and save on their prescription drug purchases in the United States. The company operates a price comparison platform that provides consumers with curated, geographically relevant prescription pricing, and access to negotiated prices. It also offers other healthcare products and services, including subscription programs and pharma manufacturer solutions, as well as telehealth services through the GoodRx Care platform. In addition, the company provides healthcare products and solutions for dogs, cats, and other pets. It serves pharmacy benefit managers who manage formularies and prescription transactions, including establishing pricing between consumers and pharmacies. The company was founded in 2011 and is headquartered in Santa Monica, California.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Wendy  Barnes | President, CEO & Director | Age 52 | Compensation: $3.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 697 people. Revenue per employee of $1.1M ranks in the top quartile among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 8%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $236K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $110K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["GoodRx Holdings, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $826M market cap on $797M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory. Operating margins are expanding by +12.2pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $164M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 21 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 5.52\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 2.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 26.2% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 12% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $9.7M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-9678712.2},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 11% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 75% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 59% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (25.6% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"GoodRx (GDRX) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/goodrx-gdrx-q3-2026-earnings-154328000.html","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795622233.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.34,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Here's What Key Metrics Tell Us About GoodRx (GDRX) Q3 Earnings","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3034839/here-s-what-key-metrics-tell-us-about-goodrx-gdrx-q3-earnings?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cnfm-3034839","date":"2026-11-24","timestamp":1795557601.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentim